Hewo everyone, and welcome back to a long overdue post from yours truly
I know it’s been a while since I last made one of these (9 days to be exact) but in that time, surprisingly
a lot has been happening and I’m here to break it all down for ya
I’m, of course, talking about anything Friday Night Funkin’ related, in case the name of this repo wasn’t making that clear enough
As for me, I’m doing fine, but enough of the intro, let’s talk about all that is new in the FNF community

First of all, yesterday was the release of the Funkin Mobile Trailer after the game was officially released on July 15th
Before the trailer, there were many who pre-registered for the game’s launch, myself included, and played the game on the first day
Not gonna lie, the controls are kinda janky (I’ll talk about FNF Mobile in another post, because there’s so much to unpack there)
But the trailer was what I was really waiting for, the event that would make the launch even more special
(Said trailer helped the game to reach #1 in the Apple App Store for the USA, surpassing even ROBLOX)
It also introduced most people to the wonderful world of Dariacore and Red Dante’s “Do or Die” (which was remixed by cub, another Funkin Mobile dev)
And also the beginning of the trailer brought some new animation specifically for Funkin, including canon confirmation that BF has an attitude 

In other news, there is now a new campaign launched by Makeship on behalf of the Funkin’ team with 3 new plushies to buy
The entire package costs around $90, with each plushie costing around $27 
The three characters include the long awaited-for Pico, the pyromanic Darnell, and the psycho-killer Nene
Might I be the not the first to say that these plushies are so frickin’ adorable
And this coming from a franchise that strives on making very clear it’s for ADULTS not kids
(which, by the way, Funkin’ Mobile is not rated M but T, mainly because all the naughty words were auto-censored
I guess they’re reaching for the Teen audience too, huh, ah well)
The character descriptions for these cute plushies are fine, I guess, but it seems mainly based on Pico’s School lore, especially Nene’s
If you want to see the campaign, just go to the Makeship website, and look in the featured creators tab for Friday Night Funkin’
They’ve already done a launch for this year, believe it or not, for April 1st (Those Bootleg plushies haunt my memories each day I know they exist)

In long anticipated await, the desktop version and Windows/Linux versions have been updated to match the Mobile edition FINALLY
As of writing this post, all 4(?) versions of FNF are running 0.7.3, which helped to reduce stuttering for Freeplay and the Character Select screen
The new scrolling system for Freeplay is GOATED, honestly, I don’t mind if it’s slow, and they also fixed the “disappearing rankings” problem too finally
Go and play the desktop release if you want to, link is in the README as well as “Important Links”

The final thing I want to announce is that finally, over 4 months later, we finally get a new Funkin blog, written by Moondroid
Moondroid was one of the head developers for Funkin’ Mobile, and let’s just say that the process wasn’t easy
To summarize it up, they had to rebuild FNF from the ground up with all-new code that is to be supported on touch-screens
HaxeFlixel, the game engine that FNF uses, was not meant to include the phones so needless to say, it was a difficult process
I highly encourage you to go and read that blog if you’re interested in how the Mobile port came together

That is all for the week of July the 22nd (unless I make the Funkin Mobile post, perhaps I will)
